WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:04.050
There is nothing that
makes me happier than biting

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:06.510
into a fresh piece of bread.

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:09.570
This slice is
absolutely fabulous.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:12.750
In 1932, my grandfather,
Pierre Poilâne,

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.540
started his very first bakery.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.410
For over 88 years, my
grandfather, my father, and I

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:23.220
have nurtured half a dozen
shops between Paris and London,

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.360
baking between three
and five-thousand loaves a day.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.120
When I was 16, my
mother suggested

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.430
that I start my apprenticeship.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:35.250
While I was finishing
up my apprenticeship,

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.850
my parents passed away
in a helicopter accident.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:42.100
The next day, instead of
going down to the bake house,

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.400
I went up to my father's desk.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.702
And here I was in
charge of Poilâne.

00:00:48.702 --> 00:00:50.480
In this class, I
will be teaching

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.400
you breads that we
do at the bakery.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.590
But the most important
lesson I will teach you

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:57.860
is how to attune
your five senses.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:01.160
When you're baking bread, you
have four ingredients-- water,

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.730
flour, salt, and a rising agent.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.440
You're going to learn
how to bake breads

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.990
using sourdough, wheat, rye--

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:11.990
learning how to start
your very own starter.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:16.370
We will be baking breads of
yeast, pain de mie, cornbread,

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:20.540
brioche, and also what to do
with breads, from its freshest

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:21.680
to its stalest.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:22.710
Don't be afraid.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:23.480
It's very easy.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:26.090
Do not to be discouraged
by failed attempts.

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:27.830
That's what your
journey is about.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:33.200
Baking really is an essential
and beautiful craft.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.650
Practice these recipes.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:35.520
Share them.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:40.288
Spread the love and
enjoy every single step.

00:01:40.288 --> 00:01:41.580
Je m'appelle Apollonia Poilâne.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:45.400
Et ceci est ma MasterClass.

